          "date": "2026-09-10 17:50:49.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "subject": "LU-19794 csdc: use acomp compression API",
        "message": "LU-19794 csdc: use acomp compression API\n\nFor kernels 6.15 and beyond use the acomp compression API with DMA\nsource and destination virtual addresses, instead of the legacy comp\nAPI which was removed there.\n\nThe acomp request allocation returns NULL on failure, so the\nallocation checks test for NULL and fail with -ENOMEM. The buffers\nhanded to the request are vm_map_ram() mappings or large pool\nallocations, which are not usable for DMA, so they are set with the\nnon-DMA variants of the request setters.\n\nTest-Parameters: forjanitoronly\nSigned-off-by: Nikos Papakonstantinou <npapakonstantinou@ddn.com>\nSigned-off-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I1fa60a7a933e6cdd2baa525d0520e7372def29df\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
